---@alias launchdarkly.EnvironmentReleasePhaseStepsList launchdarkly.ReleaseStep[]

---@alias launchdarkly.EnvironmentReleasePhasesList launchdarkly.EnvironmentReleasePhase[]

---How to resolve each phase of the release when you stop it:
---
---- `roll_forward_all_phases`: All phases serve the target variation.
---  Pending phases stay on the flag and are enabled.
---- `roll_forward_current_phase_and_remove_pending_phases`: Current and
---  completed phases serve the target variation. Pending phases are
---  removed.
---- `roll_back_all_phases_and_remove_pending_phases`: Current and
---  completed phases serve the original variation. Pending phases are
---  removed.
---- `roll_back_current_phase_and_remove_pending_phases`: The current
---  phase serves the original variation, and completed phases keep
---  serving the target variation. Pending phases are removed.
---
---For a single-phase release there are no completed or pending phases,
---so the two roll-forward values are equivalent, as are the two roll-back
---values.
---
---The `current_phase` values return `400` if the release is between
---phases. Use an `all_phases` value instead. A terminal release returns
---`200` unchanged for every resolution.
---@alias launchdarkly.EnvironmentReleaseResolution "roll_forward_all_phases"|"roll_forward_current_phase_and_remove_pending_phases"|"roll_back_all_phases_and_remove_pending_phases"|"roll_back_current_phase_and_remove_pending_phases"

---One step of a phase's rollout schedule.
---@class launchdarkly.EnvironmentReleaseStepInput
---@field allocation number Thousandths of a percent. `100000` is 100%, and `10000` is 10%. Guarded releases cannot exceed `50000`, preserving a control group. Each step's allocation must be greater than the previous step's. In a progressive release, an allocation of N% serves the target variation to N% of the phase's contexts and the original variation to the rest. In a guarded release, it serves the target variation to N%, the original variation to another N% as the measured control group, and the original variation to the rest without measuring them.
---@field durationMillis number

