---@class launchdarkly.PatchAIConfigRequest
---@field projectKey string The project key
---@field configKey string The AI Config key
---@field defaultVariationKey? string Key of the variation this config serves by default
---@field description? string A description of the AI Config
---@field maintainerId? string The ID of the member who maintains this resource
---@field maintainerTeamKey? string The key of the team that maintains this resource
---@field name? string A human-readable name for the AI Config
---@field tags? launchdarkly.PatchAIConfigRequestTagsList Tags for this resource
---@field evaluationMetricKey? string Evaluation metric key for this config
---@field isInverted? boolean The success direction of a judge. Offline evaluations use it to decide whether a score passes. - `true`: A lower score is better. Use this for a judge that scores bad output, such as a toxicity or hallucination judge. - `false`: A higher score is better. Use this for a judge that scores good output, such as an accuracy or relevance judge. Send this field only when the AI Config's `mode` is `judge`. If you omit it, the current direction does not change. For a built-in judge key, the API always returns the built-in direction. Built-in judge keys are `ld-ai-judge-accuracy`, `ld-ai-judge-relevance`, and `ld-ai-judge-toxicity`, with or without a `-<timestamp>` suffix such as `ld-ai-judge-accuracy-1760000000000`. The API returns a `400` error in these cases: - `isInverted is only supported for judge mode`: You send this field and the AI Config's `mode` is `agent` or `completion`. Remove the field. - `isInverted is not supported`: Custom judges are not available for your account. Remove the field from the request.

---Tags for this resource
---@alias launchdarkly.PatchAIConfigRequestTagsList string[]

